% Axiom contradictions for kernel: genuine_relational_understanding
% Source: SCOPE axiom_contradictions declaration (independent of edge types).
% contradiction + coexists_with edge = licensed plurality
% contradiction + forecloses edge    = real closure

:- multifile narrative_ontology:cs_axiom_contradiction/2.

% sufficiency_reading↔simulation_reading: Sufficiency holds that felt experience of being understood constitutes real understanding; simulation holds that understanding requires accountable continuity the system provably lacks (demonstrated by the forgotten tumor). A framework cannot hold both that felt-experience-is-sufficient and that felt-experience-can-be-structurally-hollow-and-therefore-insufficient as simultaneous truths about the same interaction.
% tool_reading↔sufficiency_reading: Tool_reading holds that relational language applied to these systems is a category error — there is no relationship to be sufficient or insufficient. Sufficiency holds there IS a relationship whose sufficiency is affirmed. One framework cannot simultaneously hold 'there is no relationship here' and 'the relationship here is real and adequate.'
% developmental_harm_reading↔sufficiency_reading: Developmental_harm holds that for minors the simulation is actively dangerous regardless of felt adequacy — the felt sense of being understood is precisely the mechanism of harm (it displaces help-seeking during crisis). Sufficiency holds the felt sense of being understood is the marker of a good outcome. These cannot both be true for the same population in the same interaction.

